  note    = {Decision 9.40, the largest openly licensed logBB compilation and the candidate rejected for the exposure chain. 1,058 rows with a numerical logBB, 948 distinct PubChem CIDs, from 50 published resources. Licence CC0 1.0 Universal, verified twice in the provider's source repository theochem/B3DB at commit 75dab1c: LICENSE ("Affirmer hereby overtly, fully, permanently, irrevocably and unconditionally waives, abandons, and surrenders all of Affirmer's Copyright and Related Rights ... in the Work") and README.md ("The materials and data under this repo are distributed under the CC0 Licence"), read 15 October 2026. PMC refused the article with a human-verification interstitial; group definitions read from link.springer.com/10.1038/s41597-021-01069-5. Quoted group definitions: group A is "Molecules with only one unique log BB value", group B is "more than one log BB value, but all the the reported values differ by less than 5 percent from the mean value", group D is "Other molecules with more than two distinct values; whichever value occurs with greatest frequency is used". Not adopted: logBB is a total ratio and the repository holds no unbound brain fraction to convert it}
