  doi     = {10.1002/jps.22442},
  note    = {Decision 9.40. Valuable not for its model but for its design filter, which is the discipline B3DB lacks. Quoted: "A data set consisting of 470 experimental log BB values determined in rodents was compiled and verified to ensure that selected data represented drug disposition governed by passive diffusion across blood-brain barrier", and it corrects logBB for the unbound fraction in plasma to isolate brain tissue binding, which it then predicts from octanol/water logP and pKa. That prediction is the QSAR the exposure chain would have to adopt to use any total ratio. Read from the Consensus MCP abstract, 15 October 2026}
